<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · office</p><h1 class="enc-title">Phra Khlang</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Phra Khlang was the Siamese minister of the treasury, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/departement">department</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> and early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a> kings also managed royal trade, the ports and relations with foreign merchants and states. Holders of the office, such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kosa-pan">Kosa Pan</a>, were among the most powerful officials of the kingdom, and Europeans often called the minister the 'Barcalon'.</p></div>
